Isobar
=======

Isobar is a cross-platform WEFAX (emission F3C) weather-fax decoder that
reimplements the behavior of, and is fully interoperable with, KG-FAX v1.1.3
(K.G, 2009) — including its `.syn` file format, settings (`.ini`) schema,
and UI workflow.

Original work
-------------
All source code in this project is original, written from a functional
specification derived from reverse engineering. No code, text, or graphical
assets were copied from the original program. Where the implementation
necessarily converges with the original (e.g., the Hilbert/atan2 FM
demodulation approach, the WEFAX sync-tracking algorithm), that convergence
reflects the small number of natural implementations of a public standard
under the merger doctrine, not copying.

Provenance
----------
WEFAX (Weather Facsimile) is an international transmission standard published
by the World Meteorological Organization (WMO) and the International
Telecommunication Union (ITU):
  - FM subcarrier: 1500 Hz = black, 2300 Hz = white (ITU-R F.460).
  - Drum speeds: 60 / 120 rpm; IOC 288 / 576.
  - Start tone 300 Hz, stop tone 450 Hz.

These standards are free for anyone to implement.

KG-FAX is freeware, © K.G, 2009. It is NOT open source. The Isobar project
is independent and NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from KG-FAX.

Interoperability
----------------
Isobar reads and writes KG-FAX `.syn` files and the `kgfax.ini` settings
file for interoperability only. The `.syn` format (including its radix-255
line-count encoding) and the ini key names (including their original
spellings) are reproduced exactly because file-format interoperability
requires it.

